# Jak 3: Daxter's maze game in Vin's room (LIST-0.1.9 item 12; a tester: "the daxter pacman like minigame cant be seen
# if your set to 1st person, and you have to look down to play it in 3rd person"), run with JAKVR_TEST_TASK=51
# (city-power-game, its continue vinroom-start) QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000 JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1. A new game into play (as jak3_shadow_walk.sim),
# the task's continue, A (Cross) between the Ys until 4100 to close the new game's save notice (sim pg, build 123: it
# stayed up over Vin's room and hid the maze), Y (the game's Triangle) by the machine every 200 frames until the game starts, then Daxter
# steered round the board by the left stick, a picture every 300 frames with the head level, and some with it 30
# degrees down and 30 to the side. Expect "[vr-view] a view from the game's own camera" and "the view tipped N
# degrees down", "view in play: third person", and in the level-head pictures the board ahead, its far side up; at the
# end "the view level again" and first person back.
# 0.1.9: with QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000, the game from frame 10000 counts from the task aid's mark (Jak 2 s in
# play at the task's continue, "[vr] test: the task's set-up done"): the task's two continues load in a
# different time each run (sims pg in batch62 and 65 pressed before Vin's room was there).
# 0.1.9 (sim s10 pg on build 128b): the maze game is already on at the mark (the view tipped 63 degrees down before it)
# and the A and Y presses that were to start it quit it (Y is its Triangle): none now, Daxter steered from 10300.
